=== http_client_retry.buff — retry + exponential backoff ===
backoff schedule:
  attempt 0 -> 100ms
  attempt 1 -> 200ms
  attempt 2 -> 400ms
  attempt 3 -> 800ms

scenario A: [500, 503, 200]
[replay] status 500 -> retry; sleeping 100ms (attempt 0)
[replay] status 503 -> retry; sleeping 200ms (attempt 1)
[replay] status 200 -> ok; done after 2 retries
  total retries before success: 2

scenario B: [404]
[replay] status 404 -> fatal; aborting (no retry)
  total retries before abort: 0

scenario C: [500, 502, 503, 504]
[replay] status 500 -> retry; sleeping 100ms (attempt 0)
[replay] status 502 -> retry; sleeping 200ms (attempt 1)
[replay] status 503 -> retry; sleeping 400ms (attempt 2)
[replay] status 504 -> retry; sleeping 800ms (attempt 3)
[replay] exhausted 4 retries without success
  total retries before exhaustion: 4

live entrypoint fetch_with_retry(url, max_attempts) is documented above;
it is not called here so the golden output stays deterministic.
